## an instrument constant within every level, beside one that varies
y ~ w + x with fe: g and instruments: x ~ zg + z1
note: `zg` is absorbed by fe: g and was dropped from the instruments
fitted: 2 estimates on 12 rows, 0 singletons

## the only instrument constant within every level
y ~ w + x with fe: g and instruments: x ~ zg
error[Z0804]: the model is under-identified: 0 excluded instruments remain for 1 instrumented regressor
 --> t.zeff:1:11
  |
1 | let m = d.ivreg(y ~ w + x, fe: g, instruments: x ~ zg)
  |           ^^^^^ fewer instruments than instrumented regressors
  |
  = help: each instrumented regressor needs at least one instrument that is not a regressor of the formula
  = help: `zg` is absorbed by fe: g and was dropped from the instruments

## a fixed effect that is a regressor
y ~ w + x with fe: w and instruments: x ~ z1
error[Z0401]: `w` is a fixed effect of `fe:` and a variable of the formula too
 --> t.zeff:1:11
  |
1 | let m = d.ivreg(y ~ w + x, fe: w, instruments: x ~ z1)
  |           ^^^^^ absorbed and in the model
  |
  = help: an absorbed effect cannot be a regressor or the outcome as well; drop it from `fe:` or from the formula

## a fixed effect that is an instrument
y ~ w + x with fe: g + z1 and instruments: x ~ z1 + z2
error[Z0401]: `z1` is a fixed effect of `fe:` and an instrument too
 --> t.zeff:1:11
  |
1 | let m = d.ivreg(y ~ w + x, fe: g + z1, instruments: x ~ z1 + z2)
  |           ^^^^^ absorbed and an instrument
  |
  = help: an absorbed effect cannot be an instrument as well; drop it from `fe:` or from the instruments

## a fixed effect that is instrumented
y ~ w + x with fe: x and instruments: x ~ z1
error[Z0401]: `x` is a fixed effect of `fe:` and a variable of the formula too
 --> t.zeff:1:11
  |
1 | let m = d.ivreg(y ~ w + x, fe: x, instruments: x ~ z1)
  |           ^^^^^ absorbed and in the model
  |
  = help: an absorbed effect cannot be a regressor or the outcome as well; drop it from `fe:` or from the formula

## every row a singleton
y ~ w + x with fe: id and instruments: x ~ z1
error[Z0801]: no row remains to fit the model: every row is a singleton of fe: id
 --> t.zeff:1:11
  |
1 | let m = d.ivreg(y ~ w + x, fe: id, instruments: x ~ z1)
  |           ^^^^^ nothing to estimate within the effects
  |
  = help: an effect whose every level has one row absorbs every row; use a coarser effect, or leave it out

## a fixed effect that is not a variable
y ~ w + x with fe: nowhere and instruments: x ~ z1
error[Z0101]: no variable `nowhere` in `the frame`
 --> t.zeff:1:11
  |
1 | let m = d.ivreg(y ~ w + x, fe: nowhere, instruments: x ~ z1)
  |           ^^^^^ not a variable of the frame
  |
  = help: the variables of `the frame` are: y, x, w, z1, z2, g, zg, id
